  "id": "framing",
  "term": "framing",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology usage, framing means imaginatively putting ideas together into a possible whole, such as a hypothesis or a narrative. It refers to a selective, relatively free mental construction that is less tightly constrained by immediate facts than ordinary perception or belief.",
